==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Amakusa''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Amakusa''' level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Shiro is a backline attacker with fairly standard base stats and an inconvenient [[Multi-Hit]] timing, making him good mainly for tanky enemies without much range, but rather unreliable once enemies with long range and/or many knockbacks come into play. His [[Massive Damage]] ability is still an effective weapon against both Dark and Aku enemies, as he outranges many of them, although against both of his target traits he has his own issues against each. He does enough damage to stagger most Darks, but his multi-hits are too closely spaced, hence reducing his damage output as he'll just miss, and with his slow attack rate, he might not be able to catch the Dark threats in time. Aku threats are a bit different, as his [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] dismisses their common gimmick and can be paired with Surge-Immune meatshields, but [[Shield]]s often put his performance into question. It's perfectly fine against threats with very tough shields, as despite lacking Shield Piercing, he can land all his hits and deal serious damage to them anyway. For weaker Shields that he can break before landing his final hit, Amakusa can potentially land a powerful blow, which is usually enough to finish weaker Aku threats. Unfortunately, those that easily survive, such as [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]], can abuse this to regenerate their Shields and dramatically increase their overall staying power, so he still requires a fair bit of support with Shield Piercers.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Amakusa gains higher health and a substantially faster attack rate. The former is always good to have, though not by much with the relatively small increase as Amakusa relies on his range and Surge Immunity to stay safe. On the other hand, the attack rate boost does not solve any existing problems Amakusa had, but does provide a major increase to his utility as he is able to inflict much more damage overall. With how aggressive Dark and certain Aku enemies tend to push, his faster attack rate allows him to catch threats that are knocked back in time and reduces their chances of reaching him, and the DPS increase becomes even higher on enemies that don't stagger easily from attacks.

Additionally, Immortal Amakusa gains an accounting combo with [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera Cat]] and [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Awakened Musashi]] which increases resource drops from enemies by 30%, a high number relative to its slot count. If you don't mind the expensive evolution costs of Musashi and Amakusa, this True Form could turn useful even if just for the combo.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Dodge]]''' is the main highlight of Amakusa's Talent lineup. When fully levelled up, Amakusa has a 20% chance to dodge Dark and Aku attacks for two seconds. While this would be beneficial to protect Amakusa from things like Waves and Explosions, or superbackliners that outrange him like [[Director Kurosawah]], the main problem with this Talent is that both the proc chance and the length of the Dodge are too low. At most, if you want to improve Amakusa's survivability, get this Talent to level 1, since the only thing upgrading this Talent does is increase the Dodge's length. For 75 NP, giving Amakusa a decent chance to Dodge attacks, even if only for a brief second isn't that bad.

'''[[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]]''' is honestly quite strange. While there are a good selection of Dark and Aku enemies that can Freeze, like [[THE FOLIVOREAN]], [[Ackey]], [[Prof. Owlbrowley]], and [[Omens]], many of the enemies are poor matchups for Amakusa. For example, Omens naturally outranges Amakusa, and Ackey is a backliner with a strong Shield. The main application of this Talent is to protect Amakusa from [[Wicked Face]]'s Mini-Waves as well as to enable him to work on any Henry stage, which is still a small pool to work with. Overall, not the greatest Talent.

'''Recover Speed Up''' is genuinely terrible. For a huge NP cost, Amakusa's cooldown improves by a few seconds. On an Uber with a two minute cooldown. Do not get this under any circumstance.

Finally, Amakusa gets his stat talents. The main Talent for interest is Attack Up. On any kind of nuker, getting higher damage is always beneficial.

